<title>USA: U.S. April PPI energy goods prices.</title>
<headline>U.S. April PPI energy goods prices.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department reported energy components of the producer price index as follows, with comparisons (1982=100 unless stated otherwise).</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 May    Apr    May97/96</p>
<p> Finished Energy Goods    -2.1   -2.6     -3.1</p>
<p> -Gasoline		    -7.1   -4.1     -9.7</p>
<p> -Heating Oil		  2.2    1.4     -4.8</p>
<p> -Residential Gas-Y	 -1.3   -3.3	0.3</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1990=100.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 May    Apr    May97/96</p>
<p> Intermed.Energy Goods    -1.9   -2.0     -4.9</p>
<p> -Liq.Petroleum Gas-Z     -9.2   -5.3     -1.7</p>
<p> -Jet Fuel		    -6.2   -6.1    -15.0</p>
<p> -Diesel Fuel		 -2.7   -0.3    -14.0</p>
<p> -Residual Fuel-Z	   13.4   -7.2     -8.6</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 May    Apr    May97/96</p>
<p> Crude Energy Materials    3.4   -5.2     -2.3</p>
<p> -Coal-Z			-6.4    5.2     -2.2</p>
<p> -Natural Gas-Z		5.8  -13.3     -3.2</p>
<p> -Petroleum-Z		  7.3   -0.4     -1.3</p>
<p>Note-Crude energy materials include crude petroleum. Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
</text>
